    note right of STARTED
        OTP issuance and consumption lock this parent first.
        Existing terminal and discarded parents reject without OTP mutation.
        Overdue nonterminal parents use the named expiry and terminal cleanup before refusal.
        Issuance and verification recheck the Ticket database clock after Contact locking.
        Source OTP consumption and bounded immutable verification proof commit together.
        Post-OTP verification, guardrail, checkpoint and requirement clearing share one Ticket transaction.
        The separate signup OTP proof axis does not authorize an HTTP phase regression.
        Telephone OTP success retains the signed flow binding into the guard checkpoint.
        Durable account completion ends the sign-up flow.
        The caller then enters ordinary sign-in admission.
        IDs 70, 80 and 900 are historical tombstones;
        no duplicated handoff edge or from_signup branch exists.
    end note
